WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Failure to verified fix: a recorded Ordinum run. Planted defect in our client path, not a PocketBase bug.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:19.000
System: PocketBase 0.40.6, unmodified. Property read_authz: responses contain only records the stored rule allows. The planted defect is a stale read cache in Ordinum's client path.

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:37.299
ordinum verify runs a fault-injection campaign on the affected and the fixed build. Real output, replayed at 20×; the clock shows real elapsed time (about 5.5 minutes).

4
00:00:37.299 --> 00:00:41.699
Verdict: FIX_VERIFIED, exit 0. Every confirmed violation is fixed on the declared fixed build.

5
00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:46.099
read_authz was exercised in 100 of 100 runs on each build, so the passing result is not vacuous.

6
00:00:46.099 --> 00:00:50.499
The read_authz failure was confirmed 5 times out of 5.

7
00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:54.899
Minimization: one fault, verified 1-minimal.

8
00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:59.299
Affected build violated it 10/10, the fixed build 0/10 (one-sided Fisher p = 5.41e-06).

9
00:00:59.299 --> 00:01:10.490
ordinum ci re-runs the two saved regression cases against both builds. Real output, replayed at 4×.

10
00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:14.990
2 cases, 2 PASS: the regression expectations hold.

11
00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:27.990
Shows: campaign to verified fix in one run. Does not show: a PocketBase bug, a third-party discovery, or results beyond one host.

12
00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:34.990
Inspect the report, cases and logs at ordinum.org/evidence/pocketbase-verified-fix.
